<!--
    kuna-loweredswitchbits: a switch lowered to bit tests re-rolls
    (option loweredswitchbits).

    The bytes run from free_node_as to cmark_chunk_free of swift-cmark 0.29.0.gfm.13 (BSD-2-Clause),
    built by clang for arm64-apple-ios at -O2 -fno-inline.  The source is a
    switch on the 16-bit node->type with twelve case labels and three
    bodies.  clang tests type - 0xc001 &lt;= 11, then 1 &lt;&lt; (type - 0xc001)
    against the masks 0xc19 and 0x320, then compares 0x8005, 0x8006,
    0x8007 and 0x800b.  loweredswitch reads only compares of the selector
    against a constant and keeps the if chain.

    Stage: P2, ActionLowerSwitchDetect.  Every value of the 16-bit selector
    is run through the tests; the return path takes the most values and is
    the default, the twelve other values are cases.  Pass 1
    (loweredswitchbits off) prints the bit tests; pass 2 (on, the default)
    a switch with every case label.  The off pass runs first: an installed
    switch stays for the function for the rest of the session.
-->
